a has won multiple  costumes over her various TV appearances  but when she first appeared in the  comics in 1983 she had a red and yellow  costume with ridiculous pointed  shoulders and fur topped shoes you know  the least stealthy martial arts costume  possible over time she toned it down  into a red and gold armor deal with a  domino mask but it's katanas completely  revamped new 52 look that appeared on  screen Garen fuga horiz rendition of  katana still changes things up in a few  key ways her screen costume is a bit  more conservative than the skin tight  leotards katana wears in the comics  instead opting for a loose-fitting plain  t-shirt and pass she also doesn't have  traditional samurai shoulder guards  instead wearing a varsity style jacket  featuring floral tributes to a heritage  even with these changes katana is still  pretty recognizable Slipknot one of the  most significant design departures in  Suicide Squad can be found in Adam  Beach's version of  at night the movies costumes crew almost  totally dumped the characters comic  appearance a full muscle hugging  bodysuit with bizarre side windows loose  sleeves and a mask in the movie Slipknot  got a much more militaristic suit gone  was the corny nurse designer on his  chest instead he was decked out in  useful utility gear and a built-in  rappelling harness and his hair was tied  back to look like what else  ROK's can't said the guy doesn't have a  theme it's too bad he was only on screen  for about three minutes rick flagg Joel  Kinnaman interpretation of Rick Flagg is  relatively faithful to the modern  version of the character but there is  still a handful of small style changes  as a member of the US Army Special  Forces the comics version of Rick Flagg  keeps a close shave most of the time  whereas the movie version has a little  more going on under his nose Kinnaman is  also a living breathing human so he's a  little less beefy than the flag familiar  to DC readers however just like his  paper bound predecessor in the role  Kinnaman stake tended to wear the same  army green jumpsuit and battlefield  grade arms and of course the low guard  buzz cut that serves as a not-so-subtle  salute to his military service Amanda  Waller just as in the comics Amanda  Waller is the tough assembler of Task  Force X who in actress Viola Davis words  is a big powerful black woman hard and  ready to pick up a gun and shoot anyone  at will unlike many of the other  characters in Suicide Squad Davis's  version of Waller bypassed DC Comics  reboot new 52 renditions of her  character and went all the way back to a  earlier more business-oriented look like  in her 1980s legends debut her pearls  and hairdo for example were pretty close  replicas of some of the earliest  appearances the Joker while Jared Leto's  version of the Joker adopted some of the  comics versions physical characteristics  it was also a new take on the character  in several noticeable ways while Leto  did key  The Joker's bright green do he slicked  it down instead of the more unkempt  approach often favored by the classic  Joker Leto's Joker assured in the era of  the character with grilled teeth and  threatening tattoos and while we don't  get to see the Joker's bare back sad  photos and statues based on the movie  revealed a dragon tattoo that looks  pretty similar to the one Joker has in  all-star Batman and Robin even his  signature purple coat got a biker  friendly update rather than the playful  suit styling a bold he had a shiny  alligator skin number and went shirtless  beneath just in case people wanted to  see that he wrote his own name on his  stomach you know just in case you forgot  or just got lost in a mall Harley Quinn  margot robbie hit a home run as the bat  wielding harley quinn but the character  is hardly recognizable as the one that  debuted in Batman  the animated series the old Harley Quinn  looks like a straight-up jester which we  got to see on-screen during Suicide  Squad for one hot second  but it's the later versions of the  character that lent a great deal to  Harley's movie look Robbie is a  postmodern Punk complete with colourful  pigtails messy makeup tattoos and a  getup that should appeal to cheerleaders  and biker chicks alike the pigtails are  borrowed specifically from Harley's  appearance in the video game Batman  Arkham City and the tattered t-shirt is  pure injustice gods among us and we can  thank a new 52 solo title for those  shorts Killer Croc the appearance and  origin story of Killer Croc have changed  so many times over the years that  there's really not one true croc but the  guy we see in Suicide Squad is  surprisingly true to his very first full  appearance in Batman number 358 where  he's just a guy with this skin condition  during his first appearance he showed up  in a standard mobster trench coat and  hat and sambal in Suicide Squad he's  wearing a hoodie which is pretty much  the modern equivalent  one as time goes by in the comics Crocs  slowly devolves into a more brutish  animalistic villain sprouting a tail and  long reptilian snout so while the  cinematic counterpart seems to be a  relatively regular guy now the future  isn't looking too bright sorry dude  Deadshot it's hard to hide a face as  marketable as well Smith's so it's no  wonder the Suicide Squad version of  Deadshot doesn't often wear his  trademark mask when he does put it on  the on screen version flips the script  and places his fancy site over wills  left eye whereas comics Deadshot favors  the right it's a relatively small  difference compared to the big picture  however on screen he wears a uniform  that looks like riot gear and his usual  red and silver costume is nowhere to be  seen  also Floyd Lawton has traditionally been  a white guy with a doofy little mustache  honestly we prefer the fresh prints in  this instance all of this however is  light-years away from dead shots first  appearance in 1950 where he looked like  a stage magician top hat and all he  tangled with Batman once and disappeared  until 1977 when he took on his more  modern look which is still nothing like  what we see on screen enchantress in the  comics enchantress receives her powers  after wandering off into a creepy room  at a mansion party and talking to a fat  magichead in a giant chair because why  not  after blond Bob head June moon  transforms into enchantress she looks  like a standard sexy Halloween witch  brain pointed hat long cape miniskirt  and thigh high boots later as she loses  control of the palace and turns a little  evil she dons an emerald green halter  top and gold band fitted around her head  with occasional returns to her  old-school look in Suicide Squad  enchantress is an archaeologist who gets  her powers from an ancient relic  whatever got under her skin in that  creepy old temple also gave her a  complete gross makeover making a far  more darken  gee then a comics counterpart only  cleaning up a bit when her powers are at  full force the on screen inch at risk  played by Cara Delevingne wears a hunter  green swimsuit and Crescent headdress a  weird shadow of a comics counterpart and  for some reason the filmmakers decided  to make her look kind of like Pigpen  from Charlie Brown  good grief thanks for watching subscribe  to our YouTube channel to watch more  videos like the one you just saw and  leave us a comment to let us know which  costume upgrade you liked the most
 

